# Title: Potentially Suspicious Child Process Of VsCode
# ID: 5a3164f2-b373-4152-93cf-090b13c12d27
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2023-01-26
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1218, attack.t1202
# Description: Detects uncommon or suspicious child processes spawning from a VsCode "code.exe" process. This could indicate an attempt of persistence via VsCode tasks or terminal profiles.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((process.parent.executable:*\\code.exe) AND (((process.executable:*\\powershell.exe OR process.executable:*\\pwsh.exe OR process.executable:*\\cmd.exe) AND (process.command_line:*Invoke-Expressions* OR process.command_line:*IEX* OR process.command_line:*Invoke-Command* OR process.command_line:*ICM* OR process.command_line:*DownloadString* OR process.command_line:*rundll32* OR process.command_line:*regsvr32* OR process.command_line:*wscript* OR process.command_line:*cscript*)) OR ((process.executable:*\\calc.exe OR process.executable:*\\regsvr32.exe OR process.executable:*\\rundll32.exe OR process.executable:*\\cscript.exe OR process.executable:*\\wscript.exe)) OR ((process.executable:*:\\Users\\Public\\* OR process.executable:*:\\Windows\\Temp\\* OR process.executable:*:\\Temp\\*))))
